# The network of "The Friday change": the office, the data centre behind
# an inspection firewall, the store with its tills and card readers, and
# the internet beyond r1.
#
#   office 10.1.0.10 --- r1 ---- r2 (firewall) ---- r3 --- dc 10.3.0.10
#                       / | \______ emergency link ___/        (stock app :8080)
#                      /  |
#      wan 198.51.100.2   r4 --- till 10.2.0.10    (10.2.0.0/24)
#                     |      \-- reader 10.2.200.10 (10.2.200.0/24)
#   isp 198.51.100.1 --- web 203.0.113.10 (the payment provider)
#
# r1-r2 10.0.12.0/30, r2-r3 10.0.23.0/30, r1-r3 10.0.13.0/30 (the emergency
# link), r1-r4 10.0.14.0/30. Each router's interfaces are named after what
# is at the far end. There is no NAT in this topic, so the ISP carries the
# shop's private addresses back to r1. r2's firewall is its own
# /etc/nftables.conf, loaded at every boot by nftables@r2.
machine office
machine dc
machine till
machine reader
machine r1 router
machine r2 router
machine r3 router
machine r4 router
machine isp router
machine web

link office:eth0=10.1.0.10/24 r1:lan=10.1.0.1/24
link r1:r2=10.0.12.1/30 r2:r1=10.0.12.2/30
link r2:r3=10.0.23.1/30 r3:r2=10.0.23.2/30
link r1:r3=10.0.13.1/30 r3:r1=10.0.13.2/30
link r1:r4=10.0.14.1/30 r4:r1=10.0.14.2/30
link dc:eth0=10.3.0.10/24 r3:lan=10.3.0.1/24
link till:eth0=10.2.0.10/24 r4:tills=10.2.0.1/24
link reader:eth0=10.2.200.10/24 r4:readers=10.2.200.1/24
link r1:wan=198.51.100.2/24 isp:shop=198.51.100.1/24
link isp:web=203.0.113.1/24 web:eth0=203.0.113.10/24

route office default via 10.1.0.1
route dc default via 10.3.0.1
route till default via 10.2.0.1
route reader default via 10.2.200.1
route web default via 203.0.113.1
route isp 10.0.0.0/8 via 198.51.100.2

run r1 frr
run r2 frr nftables
run r3 frr
run r4 frr
run dc nginx
run web nginx
